---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Tracks Remember | A Reflective Journey Across England"
  description="A reflective travel narrative exploring memory, family, and place through a journey across England."
>
  <Hero
    title="The Tracks Remember"
    subtitle="A journey across England. A return to something deeper."
    text="A story told in two ways—through reflection and through wonder."
    primaryHref="/the-tracks-remember"
    primaryLabel="Explore the Story"
    secondaryHref="/trains-and-castles"
    secondaryLabel="Explore with Saúl"
  />

  <Section className="books-grid">
    <div class="grid two-up">
      <article class="card">
        <img
          src="/covers/tracks-remember.jpg"
          alt="The Tracks Remember book cover by Jorge R. Obando"
          title="The Tracks Remember — Jorge R. Obando"
        />
        <h2>The Tracks Remember</h2>
        <p>
          A reflective journey through memory, place, family, and meaning—told
          through landscapes, quiet observations, and the inner movement of travel.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/the-tracks-remember">Explore the Story</a>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <img
          src="/covers/trains-castles.jpg"
          alt="Trains and Castles book cover by Jorge R. Obando"
          title="Trains and Castles — Jorge R. Obando"
        />
        <h2>Trains and Castles</h2>
        <p>
          The same adventure, seen through a child’s eyes—full of trains, castles,
          questions, movement, and wonder.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/trains-and-castles">Explore with Saúl</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Two books. One journey.">
    <p>
      These two books share the same path, but not the same voice.
      One remembers. The other lives it.
      Together, they offer two ways of seeing a journey across England—through
      reflection and through wonder.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="The journey">
    <p>
      From New York to London, York, Bamburgh, Lindisfarne, Edinburgh, and back again,
      the journey moves through places filled with history, emotion, and discovery.
    </p>
    <p>
      What changes along the way is not only the landscape, but the way it is seen.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Music inspired by Bamburgh Castle">
    <p>
      During the journey, Bamburgh became one of the places that stayed with us most deeply.
      Its history, landscape, and quiet presence continue to echo beyond the pages of the books.
    </p>
    <p>
      Andy Craig, a guide at Bamburgh Castle, created <em>Bamburgh Tales</em> — music inspired by
      historical characters from the castle’s past.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can listen to and support Andy’s music on Bandcamp, and follow more of his work through
      his social pages.
    </p>
    <a
      class="button"
      href="https://andycraigsongs.bandcamp.com/album/bamburgh-tales"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      Listen to Bamburgh Tales
    </a>

    <div class="home-social-continue">
      <p>Follow Andy Craig:</p>
      <div>
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/northumberland360" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram @northumberland360</a>
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/search/top?q=Andy%20Craig%20Songs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook: Andy Craig Songs</a>
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/search/top?q=Andy%20Craig%20Photography" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook: Andy Craig Photography</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="Continue the journey">
    <p>
      Explore comics, coloring pages, bonus reflections, and more beyond the printed pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      Step inside the member space to continue the experience in a new way. This is the beginning of the digital side of the journey.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="https://bookmembers.base44.app/members">Enter the Member Space</a>

    <div class="home-social-continue">
      <p>Continue the story:</p>
      <div>
        <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/@thetracksrember" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">TikTok</a>
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/thetracksrember" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Instagram</a>
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@thetracksrember" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section title="About the author">
    <p>
      Jorge R. Obando writes about memory, movement, family, and the quiet meaning
      carried inside ordinary moments.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Tracks Remember and Trains and Castles were created as companion works—two ways
      of telling one shared journey.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="/about">About Jorge</a>
  </Section>
  
  <Section title="Beyond the journey">
    <div class="grid one-up">
      <article class="card">
        <img
          src="/covers/what-remains.jpg"
          alt="What Remains book cover by Jorge R. Obando"
          title="What Remains — Jorge R. Obando"
        />
        <h2>What Remains</h2>
        <p>
          A quiet companion work exploring memory, fragments, absence, and the pieces
          that stay with us after a moment has passed.
        </p>
        <a
          class="text-link"
          href="https://www.whatremains.site/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Visit What Remains
        </a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </Section>
    <Section>
    <div class="related-community">
      <div class="related-community-mark">LA</div>

      <div>
        <h2>Discover Local Authors</h2>

        <p>
          LocalAuthors.online helps readers discover books by writers in their community.
        </p>

        <a
          href="https://www.localauthors.online"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="related-community-link"
        >
          Visit LocalAuthors.online
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>